 Countdown to Friday begins! Today's newsletter, edited by Herb Scribner, is 977 words, a 3½-min. read. Thanks to Sheryl Miller for copy editing . 

 ⛰️ Exclusive: Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent made the case for lighter financial regulation at the G20 finance ministers gathering in the Blue Ridge Mountains today, telling CEOs that post-crisis rules have squeezed small banks.

 Bessent said in Asheville, N.C.: "To expand opportunity for all Americans, the banks that serve Main Street must have the same chance to succeed as those that serve Wall Street." More from Courtenay Brown . ⚡ Situational awareness: President Trump and his senior aides have been considering waging limited strikes in the Strait of Hormuz to curb future attacks from Iran, Axios' Barak Ravid reports .

 
 
