 2. ⛽ 100 gallons of gas on a chart 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data : U.S. Energy Information Administration. (Each week compares the cost of 100 gallons at that week's price with the cost of 100 gallons at the price at the beginning of the conflict.) Chart: Andrew Pantazi/Axios Higher gasoline prices in the first six months of the Iran conflict have cost U.S. drivers far more than they did over the same period after Russia's invasion of Ukraine, Axios' Ben Geman and Andrew Pantazi report. 

 Yes, gasoline hit an all-time high of over $5 per gallon under the Biden administration. But the elevation since the Iran war began has been more persistent. 🎨 The big picture: Axios tracked what 100 gallons of gas cost each week during the first six months of the Iran and Ukraine conflicts, compared with prices just before each war began.

 The cumulative extra cost of gasoline is substantially higher now. 👀 What we're watching: The average U.S. gasoline price hit $4.08 today, according to AAA .

 Prices will likely be near or above $4 per gallon on Labor Day weekend. Share this story ... Get Axios Future of Energy . 

 
 
