 4. 🇦🇷 1 for the road: Messi waves goodbye 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Lionel Messi in an Argentina jersey, walking off the field after the World Cup Final in July. Photo: Hannah Peters/FIFA via Getty Images Lionel Messi announced today that he's retiring from Argentina's national soccer team.

 🐐 Messi is widely regarded as one of the greatest soccer players ever, along with Pelé and Maradona. 📱 Messi wrote on his Instagram account: "It was a decision that hurt, and still hurts deeply, but I understand that the time has come."

 "I swear to you that I always gave it my all, not just in these last few years when we won everything, but before that too. I always fought and left everything on the field for this jersey, to bring you joy and make you feel proud to be Argentine through football." 🌟 Stunning stat: Messi will end his international career tied with longtime rival Cristiano Ronaldo for the most World Cup tournament appearances (six) in history, The Athletic reports ( gift link ).

